---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

/*
  NOT LEGAL ADVICE. Standard website terms for a booking site with no
  e-commerce and no accounts. Have a lawyer review before launch, particularly
  the press-asset licence, which is the clause a magazine or promoter will
  actually rely on.
*/
---

<Legal
  title="Terms of Use | DEEJAY T-JR."
  description="Terms of use for deejaytjr.com, including how press kit assets may be used."
  path="/terms"
  heading="Terms of use"
  updated="September 2026"
>
  <p>
    These terms cover your use of deejaytjr.com. By using the site you accept them. They are short
    because the site is simple: there are no accounts, nothing is sold here, and the only thing you
    can submit is a booking enquiry.
  </p>

  <h2>Booking enquiries</h2>
  <p>
    Submitting the availability form is a request, not a booking. Nothing is confirmed until we have replied and a written performance agreement is signed. Fees quoted by email are
    valid for the date and terms quoted and may change if the event details change.
  </p>

  <h2>Press kit assets</h2>
  <p>
    Photographs, logos, bios and video linked from the <a href="/press">press page</a> may be used
    without asking us first, provided the use is editorial or promotional and connected to a
    confirmed booking, an event she is performing at, or coverage of her work. Please:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Credit the photographer where a credit is listed with the image</li>
    <li>Use the logo marks as supplied, without recolouring, rotating or distorting them</li>
    <li>Format her name as DEEJAY T-JR., with the period</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Any other use — including merchandise, AI training, resale, or implying an endorsement or
    partnership that does not exist — requires written permission from us.
  </p>

  <h2>Everything else on this site</h2>
  <p>
    The design, text and code of this site are owned by DEEJAY T-JR. and her representatives. You
    may link to any page freely. Please do not copy the site’s copy or design for another
    performer’s site.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    We keep the credentials, audience figures and availability information on this site current, but
    it is provided as-is. Figures sourced from social platform analytics are accurate as of the date
    noted beside them. If something here is out of date and it matters to your decision, ask us and
    we will confirm it in writing.
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>
    This site links to and embeds third-party platforms including social networks, YouTube, Apple
    Music, Spotify and Bandcamp. We do not control those services and are not responsible for their
    content or their handling of your data.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the Province of Ontario and the federal laws of Canada
    that apply in it.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms go to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
